title: 'frame-support: make `#[stored]` work in crates without a direct `derive-where` dependency'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `#[frame_support::stored]` passes `crate = frame_support::derive_where` to `derive_where`, so
    the code it generates uses the `frame-support` re-export and compiles in crates that do not
    depend on `derive-where` directly.
crates:
- name: frame-support-procedural
  bump: patch
